  "QLD:innisfail:January": "Wet season dominates. Humidity extreme, rain heavy, fungal disease intense.\r\n\r\nCool-season crops grow well. Lettuce, Asian greens, tomatoes, capsicums produce but need disease management.\r\n\r\nDrainage critical. Succession plant rather than one heavy planting.",
  "QLD:innisfail:February": "Wet season dominates. Humidity extreme, rain heavy, fungal disease intense.\r\n\r\nCool-season crops grow well. Lettuce, Asian greens, tomatoes, capsicums produce but need disease management.\r\n\r\nDrainage critical. Succession plant rather than one heavy planting.",
  "QLD:innisfail:March": "Wet season dominates. Humidity extreme, rain heavy, fungal disease intense.\r\n\r\nCool-season crops grow well. Lettuce, Asian greens, tomatoes, capsicums produce but need disease management.\r\n\r\nDrainage critical. Succession plant rather than one heavy planting.",
  "QLD:innisfail:April": "Dry season is growing season. Consistent warmth and low humidity ideal.\r\n\r\nPlant and sow everything: brassicas, lettuce, roots, tomatoes, capsicums, beans, squash.\r\n\r\nWater essential—no dry-season rain. Dry season is productive heart.",
