  "QLD:innisfail:September": "Dry season is growing season. Consistent warmth and low humidity ideal.\r\n\r\nPlant and sow everything: brassicas, lettuce, roots, tomatoes, capsicums, beans, squash.\r\n\r\nWater essential—no dry-season rain. Dry season is productive heart.",
  "QLD:innisfail:October": "Dry season is growing season. Consistent warmth and low humidity ideal.\r\n\r\nPlant and sow everything: brassicas, lettuce, roots, tomatoes, capsicums, beans, squash.\r\n\r\nWater essential—no dry-season rain. Dry season is productive heart.",
  "QLD:innisfail:November": "Dry season is growing season. Consistent warmth and low humidity ideal.\r\n\r\nPlant and sow everything: brassicas, lettuce, roots, tomatoes, capsicums, beans, squash.\r\n\r\nWater essential—no dry-season rain. Dry season is productive heart.",
  "QLD:innisfail:December": "Wet season dominates. Humidity extreme, rain heavy, fungal disease intense.\r\n\r\nCool-season crops grow well. Lettuce, Asian greens, tomatoes, capsicums produce but need disease management.\r\n\r\nDrainage critical. Succession plant rather than one heavy planting.",
  "QLD:ipswich:January": "Summer production solid. Tomatoes, beans, cucumbers, zucchini, pumpkins grow well with consistent water. Pick regularly.\r\n\r\nSow autumn crops in warm soil: carrots, beets, brassicas, lettuce establish quickly.\r\n\r\nWater deeply morning. Mulch moderates temperature.",
  "QLD:ipswich:February": "Summer production solid. Tomatoes, beans, cucumbers, zucchini, pumpkins grow well with consistent water. Pick regularly.\r\n\r\nSow autumn crops in warm soil: carrots, beets, brassicas, lettuce establish quickly.\r\n\r\nWater deeply morning. Mulch moderates temperature.",
  "QLD:ipswich:March": "Autumn established. Prime time for cool-season crops: brassicas, lettuce, roots, peas, beans.\r\n\r\nPlant seedlings and direct-sow freely. Garlic in April. Everything grows steadily as temperatures cool.\r\n\r\nClear summer crops. Empty beds should be mulched.",
  "QLD:ipswich:April": "Autumn established. Prime time for cool-season crops: brassicas, lettuce, roots, peas, beans.\r\n\r\nPlant seedlings and direct-sow freely. Garlic in April. Everything grows steadily as temperatures cool.\r\n\r\nClear summer crops. Empty beds should be mulched.",
  "QLD:ipswich:May": "Autumn established. Prime time for cool-season crops: brassicas, lettuce, roots, peas, beans.\r\n\r\nPlant seedlings and direct-sow freely. Garlic in April. Everything grows steadily as temperatures cool.\r\n\r\nClear summer crops. Empty beds should be mulched.",
  "QLD:ipswich:June": "Winter is cool to cold. Frosts vary by location.\r\n\r\nWinter crops provide steady harvest. Kale, spinach, peas, beans, roots produce. Protect tender plantings.\r\n\r\nStart spring seedlings indoors. Prepare beds.",
  "QLD:ipswich:July": "Winter is cool to cold. Frosts vary by location.\r\n\r\nWinter crops provide steady harvest. Kale, spinach, peas, beans, roots produce. Protect tender plantings.\r\n\r\nStart spring seedlings indoors. Prepare beds.",
  "QLD:ipswich:August": "Winter is cool to cold. Frosts vary by location.\r\n\r\nWinter crops provide steady harvest. Kale, spinach, peas, beans, roots produce. Protect tender plantings.\r\n\r\nStart spring seedlings indoors. Prepare beds.",
  "QLD:ipswich:September": "Spring arrives progressively. Frost risk decreases but may linger into early October.\r\n\r\nPlant tender crops after last frost. Sow: carrots, lettuce, roots, herbs. Succession sow.\r\n\r\nGrowth accelerates through spring.",
