  "SA:port augusta:January": "Summer production solid. Tomatoes, beans, cucumbers, zucchini, pumpkins grow well with consistent water. Pick regularly.\r\n\r\nSow autumn crops in warm soil: carrots, beets, brassicas, lettuce establish quickly.\r\n\r\nWater deeply morning. Mulch moderates temperature.",
  "SA:port augusta:February": "Summer production solid. Tomatoes, beans, cucumbers, zucchini, pumpkins grow well with consistent water. Pick regularly.\r\n\r\nSow autumn crops in warm soil: carrots, beets, brassicas, lettuce establish quickly.\r\n\r\nWater deeply morning. Mulch moderates temperature.",
  "SA:port augusta:March": "Autumn established. Prime time for cool-season crops: brassicas, lettuce, roots, peas, beans.\r\n\r\nPlant seedlings and direct-sow freely. Garlic in April. Everything grows steadily as temperatures cool.\r\n\r\nClear summer crops. Empty beds should be mulched.",
  "SA:port augusta:April": "Autumn established. Prime time for cool-season crops: brassicas, lettuce, roots, peas, beans.\r\n\r\nPlant seedlings and direct-sow freely. Garlic in April. Everything grows steadily as temperatures cool.\r\n\r\nClear summer crops. Empty beds should be mulched.",
  "SA:port augusta:May": "Autumn established. Prime time for cool-season crops: brassicas, lettuce, roots, peas, beans.\r\n\r\nPlant seedlings and direct-sow freely. Garlic in April. Everything grows steadily as temperatures cool.\r\n\r\nClear summer crops. Empty beds should be mulched.",
  "SA:port augusta:June": "Winter is cool to cold. Frosts vary by location.\r\n\r\nWinter crops provide steady harvest. Kale, spinach, peas, beans, roots produce. Protect tender plantings.\r\n\r\nStart spring seedlings indoors. Prepare beds.",
  "SA:port augusta:July": "Winter is cool to cold. Frosts vary by location.\r\n\r\nWinter crops provide steady harvest. Kale, spinach, peas, beans, roots produce. Protect tender plantings.\r\n\r\nStart spring seedlings indoors. Prepare beds.",
  "SA:port augusta:August": "Winter is cool to cold. Frosts vary by location.\r\n\r\nWinter crops provide steady harvest. Kale, spinach, peas, beans, roots produce. Protect tender plantings.\r\n\r\nStart spring seedlings indoors. Prepare beds.",
  "SA:port augusta:September": "Spring arrives progressively. Frost risk decreases but may linger into early October.\r\n\r\nPlant tender crops after last frost. Sow: carrots, lettuce, roots, herbs. Succession sow.\r\n\r\nGrowth accelerates through spring.",
