  "TAS:west hobart:November": "Great planting month. Soil warm, frost risk low, everything grows confidently.\r\n\r\nPlant tomatoes, cucumbers, pumpkins, zucchini, beans. Capsicums and eggplants need warmest spots.\r\n\r\nMulch deeply. Consistent moisture prevents bitterness and blossom-end rot.",
  "TAS:west hobart:December": "Garden hits full summer momentum. Long days and warmth drive rapid growth and harvest.\r\n\r\nKeep picking beans, cucumbers, zucchini. Harvest peas before heat finishes. Succession sow fast crops.\r\n\r\nDeep morning watering and thick mulch beat frequent shallow watering.",
  "VIC:ararat:January": "Summer is milder. Growth steady but cool nights limit heat-lovers. Keep picking.\r\n\r\nStart brassica and lettuce seedlings indoors. Direct-sow carrots, beetroot, silverbeet, kale.\r\n\r\nWater deeply morning. Mulch heavily.",
  "VIC:ararat:February": "Summer is milder. Growth steady but cool nights limit heat-lovers. Keep picking.\r\n\r\nStart brassica and lettuce seedlings indoors. Direct-sow carrots, beetroot, silverbeet, kale.\r\n\r\nWater deeply morning. Mulch heavily.",
  "VIC:ararat:March": "Autumn transitions fast. Cool nights arrive, autumn crops thrive.\r\n\r\nPlant brassicas, lettuce, leeks, onions. Direct-sow roots, peas, spinach, beans. Garlic in April.\r\n\r\nClear summer crops promptly. Empty beds need compost.",
  "VIC:ararat:April": "Autumn transitions fast. Cool nights arrive, autumn crops thrive.\r\n\r\nPlant brassicas, lettuce, leeks, onions. Direct-sow roots, peas, spinach, beans. Garlic in April.\r\n\r\nClear summer crops promptly. Empty beds need compost.",
